# Isengard production environment.
#
# Loaded by docker compose at every up/restart. install/install.sh
# prompts the operator for these values on first run and writes them
# here; secret values are NEVER in this file.
#
# Secrets (Cloudflare API token, backup passphrase, ...) live encrypted
# in the controller's SQLite, keyed by /etc/isengard/master.key. Manage
# them via:
#   isd secret put <name>             # while the stack is up
#   isengard secret bootstrap <name>  # at install time, see install.sh
#
# Lines that start with `#` are comments. Don't quote values unless they
# contain spaces; docker compose --env-file follows POSIX shell-style
# parsing and `KEY=value` is the safe form.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Image tag (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pin to a tagged release for reproducibility once we ship one. Default
# is `next` (rolling).
#
# ISENGARD_IMAGE_TAG=next

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# State path (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where bind-mounted state lives on the host. Defaults to /var/lib/isengard.
#
# ISENGARD_PREFIX=/var/lib/isengard

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bind addresses (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production binds the controller's gRPC + dashboard to host loopback by
# default. Front them with a Cloudflare Tunnel or reverse proxy for
# remote access; only change these if you know exactly what you're
# exposing.
#
# ISENGARD_CONTROLLER_GRPC_BIND=127.0.0.1
# ISENGARD_CONTROLLER_HTTP_BIND=127.0.0.1
# ISENGARD_CONTROLLER_DNS_BIND=127.0.0.1
#
# The pingora proxy publishes on all interfaces by default since that's
# the whole point of a reverse proxy. Restrict to one interface if
# multi-homed.
#
# ISENGARD_PROXY_BIND=0.0.0.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker socket (optional, only for non-standard runtimes)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DOCKER_SOCK=/var/run/docker.sock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logging (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUST_LOG=info

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DNS resolver (optional, v0.3b)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Empty disables the resolver. Set to a zone name (e.g. `iso`, `weavers`,
# `lan`) to expose <host>.<zone> resolution on UDP 5300.
#
# ISENGARD_DNS_ZONE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACME / TLS  (set by install.sh from the interactive prompt)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email used as the ACME contact when the agent requests certs from
# Let's Encrypt. Required if you publish any public HTTPS routing rule.
#
ISENGARD_ACME_EMAIL=

# Comma-separated list of hostnames for which the agent should pre-issue
# certs on startup. Wildcards (*.example.com) require DNS-01 (which uses
# the bootstrapped 'cf_dns_api_token' secret).
#
ISENGARD_ACME_DOMAINS=

# ACME environment. Accepts shorthand or a raw URL:
#   staging | stage              -> LE staging (default; un-trusted by browsers)
#   production | prod | <empty>  -> LE production (real browser-trusted certs)
#   <URL>                        -> any directory URL (custom CA, Pebble, etc.)
# Resolved by the controller at boot. Flip 'staging' -> 'production'
# only after a successful staging issue + 'docker compose restart controller'.
#
ISENGARD_ACME_DIRECTORY=staging

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enrollment token (transient, optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mint with:
#   docker exec iso-controller isengard controller token mint --role agent
# Paste the token here ONLY if you want the agent to enroll on the next
# `compose up`. After successful enrollment the agent persists its mTLS
# cert and the token can (and should) be removed from this file.
#
# ISENGARD_ENROLL_TOKEN=
